> The Stdcpp target

The stdcpp (standard c++) target allows you to write command line utilities in Cerberus.

>> You will need

>> Windows Requirements

* [MinGW 4.9.2](https://www.cerberus-x.com/downloads/tdm-gcc-64.zip) or [Visual Studio Community 2019 for Windows Desktop](https://visualstudio.microsoft.com/de/thank-you-downloading-visual-studio/?sku=Community&rel=16).
*NOTES:*~n
For Visual Studio. The default is to use Visual Studio 2019, which uses v142 of the platform tool set. To select another, uncomment and set `PLATFORM_TOOLSET_VERSION` in the [[../../bin/config.winnt.txt|config.winnt.txt]] file.~n
Platform tool sets can also be set via source file preprocessor config variables. See the C++ Tool settings in [[Programming/App config settings]]~n
For Cerberus-X to find the Visual Studio build tools. You must set `MSBUILD_PATH` in the [[../../bin/config.winnt.txt|config.winnt.txt]] file to point to the MSBuild executable file. 

For MinGW, you will need to set the `MINGW_PATH` var in your [[Trans]] config file. This should point to the actual MinGW directory, not the 'bin' sub-directory.

>> Apple macOS Requirements

* [XCode](http://developer.apple.com/xcode) developer tools, and the XCode Commandline Tools. XCode is also available via the Mac 'App Store' app.

>> Linux Requirements

* GCC C/C++ Compiler.